# The second brake's allowlist on the Linux dev machine — the tracked source of /etc/fauna/privileged-install.allow
# (docs/goal/architecture/tool-installs.md § Carrying out an approved bump, the bullet
# *The second brake*). The deployed copy is the owner's alone: the fleet never widens it, and a
# line added here reaches the machine only by the owner's own copy.
#
# One line per binary package: `<package> <repository label>`. The label is the signed Release
# file's label as apt's own simulation names the version's repository (`Inst <pkg> [<old>]
# (<new> <label>:<suite> [<arch>])`), read on the machine 2026-11-16 with `apt-cache policy`. A
# foreign-architecture copy (`libc6:amd64`) is covered by its base name.
#
# Never here (the helper's tests refuse them): the kernel, the boot loader,
# ZFS, sudo, the SSH server, systemd, apt and dpkg.

# python3-system — source python3.14 (Ubuntu)
python3.14 Ubuntu
python3.14-minimal Ubuntu
python3.14-gdbm Ubuntu
libpython3.14 Ubuntu
libpython3.14-minimal Ubuntu
libpython3.14-stdlib Ubuntu

# git — source git (Ubuntu)
git Ubuntu
git-man Ubuntu

